Date: Thu, 10 Apr 2025 00:21:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Reuse DHCP IP when transitioning to Static IP

when BMC Ip source is changed from DHCP to static, the existing
DHCP-assigned IP address typically goes down, making the BMC
unreachable over out-of-band access.

This change ensures that during transition from DHCP to static mode,
the current DHCP IP address is reused as the static IP address. This
allows the user to retain connectivity to the BMC without interruption.
Later if needed, the user can update the static IP using
`ipmitool lan set addr <new-ip>` .

Tested and Verified in GH-200:
